      statement: "A schema field that consistently carries one value either should be promoted to a constant in the schema (not a per-record field) or should be expanded to carry the variation it implies. Duplicate field names across record types should either share a vocabulary or be renamed to distinguish their scopes."  # 5200
      root_cause: "Several declared schema fields populate with effectively one value across every populated record — a constant. One scope has a substantial set of metadata fields where every populated record carries the same value, suggesting either vestigial scaffolding from a partially-implemented feature or fields that should be derived rather than stored. A second scope (node-level rather than edge-level) has a similar set of zero-entropy fields. A separate but related issue: a handful of metadata field names appear on both the edge-level and node-level metadata records, with disjoint value distributions on each. The same field name carries different vocabularies depending on which record type it appears on; the dual-scope semantics are undocumented."  # 5200
